Problem 12.2:
N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) = 2NH_3(g)
Write expression for K_p in terms of Kc.
Solution: K_P = \frac{(P_{NH_3})^2}{(P_{N,})(P_{H,})^3}
\therefore K_{p} = \frac{[NH_{3}(g)]^{2}[RT]^{2}}{[N_{2}(g)]RT.[H_{2}(g)]^{3}[RT]^{3}}
\therefore K_{p} = \frac{[NH_{3}(g)]^{2}}{[N_{2}(g)][H_{2}(g)]^{3}} \times \frac{[RT]^{2}}{[RT][RT]^{3}}
\therefore K_p = K_C \times RT^{(2-4)}
\therefore K_p = K_C \times RT^2
